Hmm wait, one thing: in the linked-issue path, `armReworkLatch(ticket)` is called even when `DRY` is false and labels added — good. But what about the GUEST PR case (cIsMachinePr false)? `armed` stays true (initialized true) → armReworkLatch(ticket) arms the latch for a guest PR with NO leg dispatched. As analyzed — harmless because consult is machine-gated, but it does pollute the snapshot with phantom entries that live up to 45 min... Actually wait — do they get pruned? `pruneStale` prunes entries older than 45 min with no active run. A phantom guest entry with no run: at publish, evaluate → runs given → no leg run on head → age: fresh → 'in-flight' → KEPT. It stays in the snapshot until 45 min pass. Since consult is machine-gated, no suppression impact. But the conflict_rework marker scan `alreadyReported` is not latch-based. So impact = snapshot noise only. Still, it's a genuine wart worth flagging (IMPORTANT or SUGGESTION). The comment above the arm says "the PR-anchored dispatch landed" — but for guests no dispatch happened at all. The arm should be gated on `cIsMachinePr`. I'll flag as IMPORTANT (correctness of the latch semantics; no functional damage though since consumers gate on machine authorship... wait — do they? Let me double-check ALL consult sites are machine-gated:

