{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `evaluate` returns on the first `'terminated'` run without checking whether a later run is still active — order-dependent**

```js
for (var i = 0; i < runs.length; i++) {
    var effect = latchEffectOfRun(runs[i], entry.head, atMs, workflowFile);
    if (effect === 'in-flight') return 'in-flight';
    if (effect === 'terminated') return 'terminated';
}
```

If the rollup contains both a concluded leg run (post-arm) and a still-active leg run on the same head (exactly the stacked-legs shape gh-1428 produced), the verdict depends on list order: a `'terminated'` hit clears the latch while another leg is genuinely flying. GitHub returns runs newest-first, so today the active run is usually seen first and the bug stays latent — but the function's contract shouldn't rely on an external API's sort order.

Cheap, order-independent version — scan everything, let `'in-flight'` win:

```js
var terminated = false;
for (var i = 0; i < runs.length; i++) {
    var effect = latchEffectOfRun(runs[i], entry.head, atMs, workflowFile);
    if (effect === 'in-flight') return 'in-flight';
    if (effect === 'terminated') terminated = true;
}
if (terminated) return 'terminated';
```
