{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: suppression here skips `processedKeys.push(key)` — the other two suppressed arming paths push**

`conflict_rework` (line ~2414) and `fail_validation` (line ~2901) both `processedKeys.push(key)` when the latch suppresses the arm; this `continue` does not. `processedKeys` drives the rule's `limit` slot accounting and lands in the published snapshot's `tick.processed`, so an `arm_rework` tick with several latched PRs consumes no limit slots and records nothing — while the equivalent suppressions in the other paths do. No bug today (suppression arguably *shouldn't* consume budget), but the three paths should agree; whichever semantics you want, make all three identical and note it, or the next rule added will copy one of each.
